    "body": "A few answers come to mind, though note I cannot officially represent Chromium:\n1. I believe replayed draw ops should be allowed if that is possible given the other choices we make.\n2. I prefer explicit opt-in in situations like this. I presume Mozilla feel the same way. The op-in could even take something that indicates the print resolution, allowing for a backing store sized correctly, or at least an integer scale.\n3. Implicit seems bad.\n4. Some preferred resolution information in an explicit method could address this.\n5. Outside my wheelhouse.",
