    "created_at": "2026-11-19T17:29:29Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-19T17:29:29Z",
    "body": "> Should a printed canvas be allowed (or expected) to use the drawing operations instead of the bitmap?\n\nI agree explicit is nicer, the implicit `reset()` is rather weird. I'm not a huge fan of the `mozPrintCallback` API ([here](https://searchfox.org/firefox-main/rev/41b747af72d91784f78616056c2f1d6c17c01345/dom/webidl/HTMLCanvasElement.webidl#43,64-75) for context), but maybe a `mozPrintCallback` like thing that is auto-awaited is nicer?\n\nE.g. you'd write:\n\n```\ncanvas.printCallback = async function(context) {\n  await draw(context);\n};\n```\n\nRather than:\n\n```\ncanvas.mozPrintCallback = async function(state) {\n  draw(state.context).then(s => state.done());\n};\n```",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
