    "body": "Emilio's canvas.printCallback looks pretty good to me.\n\nAnd to be clear, the semantics would very roughly be \"when the document is rendered for print media; for each canvas element; if printCallback is defined, invoke it; capture the canvas for printing\"\n\nHTML-in-Canvas complicates this a bit, though printCallback could have the same timing and tree-order semantics as the `paint` event. That may be desirable as we could leverage the prose and algorithms for `paint` when defining `printCallback`. Maybe even just call it \"the `print` event\" though I'm not sure what that does for async and I would have to check whether it works for the printing rendering pipeline.\n\nOffscreen is tricky too, but I suppose you might choose not to op-in in that case.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
